cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Replication materials: Bar interval outweighs entry mechanism
  in short-horizon systematic trading
message: >-
  If you use this software or dataset, please cite it using the
  metadata from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Muhammad Ubaida
    family-names: Butt
    email: mubaidabutt@gmail.com
    affiliation: >-
      Suleman Dawood School of Business, Lahore University of
      Management Sciences
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/mubaidabutt/xauusd-systematic-study
abstract: >-
  Complete replication materials for a pre-registered study of 222
  systematic trading configurations in spot gold (XAU/USD),
  including both pre-registration protocols, the append-only trial
  registry of every configuration executed, verbatim execution
  logs, and the full analysis toolchain. No configuration cleared
  its pre-registered threshold. Price data are licensed and not
  redistributed; retrieval code is included.
keywords:
  - systematic trading
  - pre-registration
  - multiple testing
  - backtest overfitting
  - transaction costs
  - null results
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-08-19'